 - **The -40 dBFS floor** was chosen on 278 renders of the default voice and model-invented voices, replayed offline:
   - Each of the 11 collapses has 10 s with no frame above -51.7 dBFS. Each of the other 267 renders has a frame at -18.5 dBFS or louder in every 10 s, and none has a run below -40 dBFS longer than the recovering stall (7.5 s at this floor).
   - A -60 dBFS floor missed one collapse into a hum, whose frames kept rising above -60 dBFS and restarting the run, and ended another only 15.4 s late, once its hum had sunk below -60 dBFS for good. At -40 dBFS each ends 10 s after it began.
+  - Whispered and soft speech stays clear of it. Eleven renders in a cloned voice and the built-in voice, of `<whisper>`, `<soft>`, `[quietly, almost whispering]`, `[sighs]`, a bedtime story and speech turning into a whisper, each 17-35 s, all ended `stop`. Some whispered words peak below -40 dBFS (the quietest at -50.8), but louder words follow within 2.5 s at most, and every 10 s holds a frame at -34.8 dBFS or louder.
   - Speech quieter than -40 dBFS for 10 s is taken for a collapse.
 
